      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T22:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `ft98xx_alg_before`, you forcefully clear the driver\u0027s private data structure:\n\n```c\nif (fixture-\u003ealg \u0026\u0026 fixture-\u003ealg-\u003edata) {\n    memset(fixture-\u003ealg-\u003edata, 0, sizeof(struct ft_libfp_data));\n}\n\n```\n\n**Issue:** This is a severe abstraction leak. A unit test should test the API\u0027s black-box/gray-box behavior, not manually wipe its internal RAM. More importantly, **this hides bugs**. If the driver\u0027s `fingerprint_algorithm_exit()` function has a bug where it fails to properly clear internal state, this manual `memset` sweeps the bug under the rug, and the tests will pass while the real firmware fails.\n**Recommendation:** Remove this `memset`. Rely strictly on `fingerprint_algorithm_exit()` to tear down state. If removing this causes tests to fail, you have just found a bug in the actual driver\u0027s cleanup code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 120,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 120,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "b92f18bbe22e098ab8a0ac97af3f96b174d0a7c8",
