      "side": 1,
      "message": "* **Double De-initialization in `test_exit_success`:**\nIn `test_exit_success`, you explicitly call `fingerprint_algorithm_exit(fixture-\u003ealg)`. However, the teardown function `ft98xx_alg_after` also unconditionally calls `fingerprint_algorithm_exit(fixture-\u003ealg)`. This will result in a double-exit, which typically leads to memory corruption, double-frees, or assertions in the underlying driver.\n**Recommendation:** Add an `is_initialized` boolean flag to the `ft98xx_bio_alg_fixture` struct. Set it to `true` when `init` succeeds, and `false` when `exit` is called. Update `ft98xx_alg_after` to only call `fingerprint_algorithm_exit()` if `is_initialized \u003d\u003d true`.",
